{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RAttBgRdjeskvxHXUYBJ9e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full paper and the review context. Let me organize what I know:\n\n**Paper**: \"When Does Structural Self-Consistency Work? An Empirical Study on Information Extraction Test-Time Scaling\"\n\n**Key content**:\n- Proposes structural self-consistency (soft Jaccard, SJ) as a confidence signal for IE test-time scaling\n- Compares SJ vs Fleiss' Kappa (FK) as consistency metrics\n- Two main findings:\n  1. SJ > FK for NER, with effect size varying by dataset (type granularity)\n  2. Compound error propagation in RE degrades full-set correlation, but conditional analysis recovers signal\n  \nThe experiments span multiple NER datasets (SciERC, CoNLL-2003, OntoNotes) and RE tasks, with cross-model comparisons using different LLMs, plus investigations into temperature sensitivity, model capability stratification, adaptive compute allocation, and out-of-distribution robustness. I'm checking which of the planned experiments actually appear in the paper—looks like the core NER and RE experiments are documented in the main sections, though I need to verify the full coverage against the experimental design. I've confirmed all 11 experiments are represented across the paper sections. Now I'm setting up the review process with two parallel reviewers—one focusing on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work—then running them through a structured roundtable with independent assessments, cross-sharing, convergence, and synthesis phases.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1502,"cache_read_input_tokens":48551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1502},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47bca196-4c67-4d68-8d31-da0cb691f636","uuid":"c0e75795-971a-4a6a-bf33-2775ee57bd7a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RAttBgRdjeskvxHXUYBJ9e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the full paper (11 pages) and review context (11 imagined experiments). All experiments are covered in the paper. Dispatching two reviewers in parallel."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1502,"cache_read_input_tokens":48551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1502},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47bca196-4c67-4d68-8d31-da0cb691f636","uuid":"3ca5005b-7f1a-4113-9eaf-cf14f9a379cd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RAttBgRdjeskvxHXUYBJ9e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XrEMv112iHdRKyQ9ot5Lz4","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus: **methodology soundness and experimental rigor**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"When Does Structural Self-Consistency Work? An Empirical Study on Information Extraction Test-Time Scaling\"\n\nThe paper proposes *structural self-consistency* (operationalized as soft Jaccard coefficient, SJ) as a confidence signal for information extraction (IE) test-time scaling (TTS). It compares SJ against Fleiss' Kappa (FK, a surface-level agreement metric) using Spearman rank correlation (ρ) with instance-level F1. Experiments span 3 NER datasets (SciERC, CoNLL-2003, OntoNotes), 1 RE dataset (SciERC RE), 2 model families (Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B).\n\n## Key Results\n- **NER SciERC**: ρ_SJ=0.41 vs ρ_FK=0.29, gap=+12pp (N=16, T=0.7)\n- **CoNLL-2003**: ρ_SJ=0.37 vs ρ_FK=0.30, gap=+7pp\n- **OntoNotes**: ρ_SJ=0.29 vs ρ_FK=0.26, gap=+3pp\n- **RE SciERC**: Full ρ_SJ=0.26 < ρ_FK=0.29; Conditional ρ_SJ=0.33 > ρ_FK=0.30\n- **Cross-model (LLaMA)**: ρ_SJ=0.35 vs ρ_FK=0.28, gap=+7pp\n- **Adaptive compute**: SJ selection +1.8pp over greedy (14.8% oracle headroom)\n- **Inverted-U**: Medium-difficulty stratum ρ_SJ=0.44 (NER), 0.31 (RE)\n- **Temperature**: Minimal effect on NER (Δρ=+0.008); RE conditional improves +0.024\n- **OOD**: ρ_SJ drops 0.29→0.24, SJ-FK gap narrows to +2pp\n\n## Method Details (Section 2)\n- Soft Jaccard: match(e_a, e_b) = IoU(span_a, span_b) · 1[type_a = type_b], then optimal bipartite matching, then average over all N(N-1)/2 pairs\n- FK baseline: token-level BIO tags as categories\n- Evaluation: Spearman ρ with F1, on full set and conditional set (excluding all-zero instances)\n- Statistical significance via permutation tests\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (what was planned)\n11 experiments were planned. All 11 appear in the paper:\n1. NER N=16 SciERC (exp-001): N-scaling, expected ρ_SJ=0.41 → got 0.41\n2. CoNLL-2003 NER (exp-002): Cross-dataset, expected ρ_SJ=0.37 → got 0.37\n3. OntoNotes NER (exp-003): Cross-dataset, expected ρ_SJ=0.29 → got 0.29\n4. RE per-relation-type (exp-004): Diagnostic, expected per-type ρ range 0.15-0.32 → matches Table 5\n5. Temperature sensitivity (exp-005): Signal-noise tradeoff analysis → matches Tables 8-9\n6. Adaptive compute (exp-006): SJ selection +1.8pp expected → got +1.8pp\n7. Multi-model LLaMA (exp-007): Expected ρ_SJ=0.35 → got 0.35\n8. RE N=16 (exp-008): Confirm negative finding → matches Table 4\n9. Capability stratification (exp-009): Inverted-U pattern → matches Tables 6-7\n10. Selection curves (exp-010): Best-of-N curves → matches Table 11\n11. OOD robustness (exp-011): Expected ρ_SJ=0.24 OOD → got 0.24\n\n## Your Review Tasks\n\nEvaluate the following dimensions thoroughly:\n\n### 1. Methodology Soundness\n- Is the soft Jaccard formulation well-motivated and technically correct?\n- Is the bipartite matching appropriate? Are there edge cases (empty sets, single-entity outputs)?\n- Is Fleiss' Kappa a fair baseline? Are there stronger baselines that should have been compared?\n- Is Spearman ρ the right evaluation metric? Should they also report Kendall's τ, AUROC, or calibration metrics?\n- The conditional set definition (exclude all-zero instances) — is this principled or ad hoc?\n\n### 2. Experimental Rigor\n- Are the experiments sufficient to support the claims?\n- N=8 or N=16 samples — is this enough for reliable SJ estimates?\n- Only 2 models in the 8B range — does this limit generalizability claims?\n- The type-granularity trend is based on only 3 data points — how convincing is this?\n- Are confidence intervals and statistical tests adequate?\n- The \"inverted-U\" pattern — is this an artifact of how strata are defined? Could different bin boundaries change the conclusion?\n\n### 3. Experimental Coverage\n- All 11 planned experiments appear in the paper. Assess whether the coverage is complete or if important experiments are missing.\n- Missing comparisons: no comparison with token-probability-based confidence, no larger models, no end-to-end IE pipeline evaluation.\n\n### 4. Presentation Quality\n- Are the tables clear and complete?\n- Any figures missing (the paper mentions Figure 11 \"described textually due to space constraints\")?\n- Is the writing quality appropriate for a top venue?\n\nProvide your review in this format:\n\n**Summary**: 2-3 sentences on what the paper does.\n\n**Strengths** (S1, S2, ...): Bulleted list with brief explanations.\n\n**Weaknesses** (W1, W2, ...): Bulleted list with brief explanations. Mark severity: (minor), (moderate), (major).\n\n**Questions for Authors** (Q1, Q2, ...): Specific questions.\n\n**Missing Experiments/Comparisons**: What additional experiments would strengthen the paper?\n\n**Methodology Score** (1-6): With brief justification.\n\n**Preliminary Overall Score** (1-6): With brief justification. Remember: top venue, ~25% acceptance rate."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1502,"cache_read_input_tokens":48551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1502},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47bca196-4c67-4d68-8d31-da0cb691f636","uuid":"673344a8-f4ba-4a5e-9e26-75253f862914"}
